  "text": "Bage 5 03/18/9020.00 50.0 19500°clear cree\nClear Creek\nBMP: SURFACE ROUGHENING\n1.\nMETHODS: Surface roughening involves roughening previously disturbed\nsoils. Surface roughening is used to reduce the speed of runoff, increase\ninfiltration, reduce erosion, trap sediment and prepare the soil for seeding by\ncapturing moisture for the seed. The soil surface is considered roughened if\ndepressions are created 2 to 4 inches deep and spaced approximately 4 to 6\ninches apart. Revegetation is required within 30 days of surface roughening or\nthe next window of opportunity.\n2.\nMATERIALS:\n• Dozer, tracked machine or tiller.\n- Seed, mulch and/or erosion control blankets.\n3. MAINTENANCE TIPS:\n• Do not drive over areas that have been treated.\n• Revegetation must occur within 30 days or next window of opportunity.\n4. TEMPORARY OR PERMANENT USE:\n• Surface roughening is a temporary BMP until revegetation occurs.\n95",
  "text_sha256": "68c188038a27e5fc5bd50edec2d5602b5b64d8ff97a6dc26927f909a4efea068",
